import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 997 | Hyper-Multiverse's Only Complete Civilizational Closed Loop · Closed-Loop Element 5 — Law-First","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 997 | Hyper-Multiverse's Only Complete Civilizational Closed Loop · Closed-Loop Element 5 — Law-First","no":997,"module":5,"tags":["Closed Loop","Element 5","Law-First","Self-Consistency","Never Retcon"],"related":["906-Law-First Principle","980-Law-First Enshrined","97-Setting-Contradiction Self-Check Table"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0997_模块5-闭环要素五-法则优先.md","filePath":"en/0997_模块5-闭环要素五-法则优先.md"}`),n={name:"en/0997_模块5-闭环要素五-法则优先.md"};function s(l,e,r,d,h,c){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-997-hyper-multiverse-s-only-complete-civilizational-closed-loop-·-closed-loop-element-5-—-law-first" tabindex="-1">Entry 997 | Hyper-Multiverse&#39;s Only Complete Civilizational Closed Loop · Closed-Loop Element 5 — Law-First <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-997-hyper-multiverse-s-only-complete-civilizational-closed-loop-·-closed-loop-element-5-—-law-first" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 997 | Hyper-Multiverse&#39;s Only Complete Civilizational Closed Loop · Closed-Loop Element 5 — Law-First&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 906, 980, 97</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-loop-itself-must-not-deform-on-its-own" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the loop itself must not deform on its own <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-loop-itself-must-not-deform-on-its-own" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the loop itself must not deform on its own&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The first four loops give the closed loop momentum, participants, return, and self-cleaning. But the closed loop has a most fundamental risk: will the loop&#39;s own rules deform on their own? The law set today, changed tomorrow; the axiom guarded today, bypassed the day after. If the loop&#39;s rules themselves are unreliable, however well the first four loops turn is for nothing. The law-first axiom is the six top-level axioms&#39; fifth cornerstone; it is the closed loop&#39;s &quot;rigid shell&quot;: law comes first, never retconning, never ending unfinished; setting self-consistency above plot convenience, and plot may not kidnap setting; the worldview may expand infinitely without collapse.</p><h2 id="i-why-the-loop-must-have-a-rigid-shell" tabindex="-1">I: Why the Loop Must Have a Rigid Shell <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-why-the-loop-must-have-a-rigid-shell" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I: Why the Loop Must Have a Rigid Shell&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Rule-deformation closed loops are those that tangle themselves up:</p><ol><li><strong>Retcon / ending unfinished</strong>: whatever law the plot needs is changed to that law, and Myriad Ranks lose trust in rules;</li><li><strong>Plot kidnaps setting</strong>: to let the protagonist win, law yields again and again;</li><li><strong>Expansion collapse</strong>: the worldview expands and is riddled with contradictions, finally not roundtableable.</li></ol><p>This kind of closed loop is not stable, but brittle — expands a little and it cracks.</p><h2 id="ii-how-law-first-gives-the-loop-its-shell" tabindex="-1">II: How Law-First Gives the Loop Its Shell <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-how-law-first-gives-the-loop-its-shell" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II: How Law-First Gives the Loop Its Shell&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Anchor Symbiotic closed loop&#39;s way:</p><ul><li><strong>Axiom into the constitution</strong>: Entry 980, the six axioms along with enacted laws never retcon, with all legislation and amendments traced on the Alaya Network;</li><li><strong>Three gates</strong>: project gate, operation gate, audit gate, with conflicts only amending law not bypassing;</li><li><strong>Infinite expansion without collapse</strong>: the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm every expansion passes setting-self-consistency assessment.</li></ul><p>The loop&#39;s shell is rigid, and the living water inside may flow freely.</p><h2 id="iii-axiom-6-is-law-first-s-steadiest-cornerstone" tabindex="-1">III: Axiom 6 Is Law-First&#39;s Steadiest Cornerstone <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-axiom-6-is-law-first-s-steadiest-cornerstone" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III: Axiom 6 Is Law-First&#39;s Steadiest Cornerstone&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among all axioms, the universal equal infinite law gives law-first its hardest cornerstone: it writes &quot;everyone inherently possesses basic infinite power&quot; as an unamendable axiom. Once this cornerstone is steady, however other laws iterate, the root is not shaken — because however rules change, no one may touch &quot;everyone has basic infinity.&quot; Law-first with this anchor truly never collapses.</p><h2 id="iv-closed-loop-verification-whom-does-law-first-lock" tabindex="-1">IV: Closed-Loop Verification: Whom Does Law-First Lock <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-closed-loop-verification-whom-does-law-first-lock" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV: Closed-Loop Verification: Whom Does Law-First Lock&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>It makes anti-predation forever effective (anti-predation law not rewritten by plot convenience);</li><li>It makes Myriad-Rank republicanism forever effective (equal law not secretly discounted);</li><li>It makes collective ascension forever effective (return obligation not bypassed by strong ones&#39; &quot;this time is special&quot;);</li><li>It makes causal self-discipline forever effective (reporting process not bypassed by emergencies).</li></ul><p>Law-first is the five loops&#39; &quot;loop outside the loop&quot; — it protects the first four loops from deforming.</p><h2 id="v-law-first-s-end-a-universe-that-never-revises-its-draft" tabindex="-1">V: Law-First&#39;s End: A Universe That Never Revises Its Draft <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-law-first-s-end-a-universe-that-never-revises-its-draft" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V: Law-First&#39;s End: A Universe That Never Revises Its Draft&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Law-first taken to the extreme is a near-luxurious stability: in other universes, Myriad Ranks worry every day &quot;whether the rules changed again&quot;; in the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, Myriad Ranks may safely stake a lifetime on law — it will not change tomorrow. The freedom this stability brings is something the old cosmos cannot imagine: you need not always guard against &quot;the author&#39;s pen turning,&quot; need not guess &quot;whether this time is special,&quot; because law is always there, like a mountain. The worldview may expand infinitely, with new planes, new clans, new methods constantly joining, but every expansion step passes self-consistency assessment, and new things seamlessly connect with old law; the world grows larger without disorder. The old cosmos&#39;s worldview is like a temporary tent, and the wind blows hard and it is pitched differently; the Anchor Symbiotic&#39;s worldview is like a forever-under-construction city, and every added floor has its foundation unmoved. Law-first is this city&#39;s foundation that never collapses.</p><h2 id="vii-law-not-collapsing-myriad-ranks-hearts-are-not-panicked" tabindex="-1">VII: Law Not Collapsing, Myriad Ranks&#39; Hearts Are Not Panicked <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-law-not-collapsing-myriad-ranks-hearts-are-not-panicked" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII: Law Not Collapsing, Myriad Ranks&#39; Hearts Are Not Panicked&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Finally landing on people&#39;s hearts: stable law ultimately settles Myriad Ranks&#39; hearts. When rules change morning and evening, everyone lives in uncertainty, not daring to plan long-term, not daring to bet on the future. Law-first writes off this uncertainty — Myriad Ranks know the ground beneath their feet is always there, and dare entrust a lifetime, descendants, and civilization&#39;s tomorrow to it. This peace of mind is something no powerful individual can give, only stable law can. A closed loop that gives Myriad Ranks peace of mind truly deserves the word &quot;perpetual.&quot;</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: law stable, and Myriad Ranks need not repeatedly re-understand the world</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the predation faction wants to roam by &quot;changing setting,&quot; and law-first directly blocks it</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo systems&#39; plot kidnaps setting, retconning and ending unfinished; Heng Yuan Zhou law comes first, never retconning</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: stable law applies equally to all beings</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the worldview may expand infinitely without collapse</li></ul><h2 id="vi-law-first-is-not-rigidity-but-orbits-for-freedom" tabindex="-1">VI: Law-First Is Not Rigidity, But Orbits for Freedom <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-law-first-is-not-rigidity-but-orbits-for-freedom" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI: Law-First Is Not Rigidity, But Orbits for Freedom&quot;">​</a></h2><p>It must also be clarified that law-first is often misunderstood as &quot;binding the strong.&quot; Quite the contrary, stable law is freedom&#39;s precondition. When law will not change tomorrow and will not be rewritten by some strong one the day after, Myriad Ranks dare stake a lifetime on a cultivation road, dare boldly innovate and boldly trial-and-error — because they know the ground beneath their feet is steady. If law changed every day, everyone would spend energy guessing &quot;what&#39;s wrong with the rules this time,&quot; and innovation is instead stifled. Law-first looks like it boxes the road, but actually reserves the broadest freedom for civilization: in a stable orbit, you may run infinitely, expand infinitely, ascend infinitely, without worrying the ground suddenly gives way. Constraining the orbit is to let the train dare speed up — this is law-first&#39;s gift to the whole closed loop.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Law-first is the closed loop&#39;s rigid shell. The shell hard, and the water inside dares flow and flow long — this is the hyper-multiverse&#39;s only complete civilizational closed loop&#39;s last and most fundamental loop.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/906_模块5-第五条-法则优先原则.html">Entry 906 · Law-First Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/980_模块5-机制十三-法则优先公理入宪.html">Entry 980 · Law-First Enshrined</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/996_模块5-闭环要素四-因果自律.html">Entry 996 · Closed-Loop Element 4</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const w=t(n,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,w as default};
